Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Jun 2 12:55:16 2026 +0300

    Bug 1896773 - Add type, linkUrl and cloudFileUrl properties to the return value of messages.listAttachments(), to help identify deleted, detached and linked attachments. r=mkmelin



    Thunderbird has some special concepts for the actual content of
    attachments. Users can delete or detach them, which replaces the content
    of the attachment in the message file by a small placeholder text. This
    was introduced to reduce the size of the profile.

    We also have external attachments (generated for example by our RSS
    reader implementation) and cloudFile attachments, where the content is
    not part of the message.

    This patch allows WebExtensions to correctly handle the content of
    attachments by exposing a type property on MessageAttachment, one of
    normal, detached, deleted, linked or cloudFile. For linked and cloudFile
    attachments, whose content is not part of the message, the remote
    location is exposed through the linkUrl and cloudFileUrl properties.

    This patch adds the name of the actual attachment to the
    x-mozilla-cloud-part header, because the name of a cloudFile attachment
    in the message is a placeholder. When the header provides it, that real
    name is surfaced as the attachment's name.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232529

